  <data name="OnexCaption450.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Only versions newer than yours are shown (no downgrades). Experimental test builds are flagged. The signed helper downloads and runs the installer — a PowerShell window shows the progress.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption451.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Setup &amp; Onboarding</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption452.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>ONEXTweaks needs a few small tools. One click checks what's present and installs anything missing.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption453.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. Required tools</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption454.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Install the missing ones with CTW Center — it links to each vendor's own installer. This page only shows what is already there.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption455.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>We're switching from the discontinued ViGEm to VIIPER (USBIP)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption456.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>usbip-win2: Checking...</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption457.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Re-check</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption458.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>USB/IP kernel driver powering the default VIIPER controller emulation (button remapping, gyro-as-stick, Mouse Mode). Install it through CTW Center, then reboot once.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption459.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>These are checked together. „Re-check tools“ asks again after you installed something.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption460.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>HidHide: Checking...</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption461.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Hides the Claw's built-in controller while emulation runs, so games see only the virtual pad — prevents double input.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption462.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>RTSS: Checking...</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption463.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>RivaTuner Statistics Server. Draws the on-screen overlay (FPS, TDP, temps) and enforces the FPS limiter.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption464.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>PawnIO: Checking...</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption465.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Kernel sensor driver. Exposes CPU/GPU power and temperature to the overlay — without it the power readout stays at 0 W.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption466.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Re-check tools</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption467.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>HidHide, RTSS and PawnIO are official, signed third-party tools installed via winget; usbip-win2 is the signed vendor driver, downloaded on demand. Individual install / download buttons live under System → Debug → Driver dependencies.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption468.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2. Disable MSI Center M</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption469.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Checking MSI Center M...</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption470.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Disable</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption471.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>3. Enable controller emulation</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption472.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Controller emulation: off</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption473.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enable</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption474.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Set up Left MSI (Claw) button</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption475.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Assign a single-click action to the Left MSI (front) button — e.g. open the Steam menu. Opens the full setup in the Controls tab.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption476.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Set up Left MSI button →</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption477.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Auto Jump to Clawtweaks on Gamebar Open</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption478.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Right MSI button opens Game Bar (its press action is unchanged). When controller emulation is active, ONEXTweaks then auto-jumps to its widget slot on open. Set this to ONEXTweaks' actual position (usually #3 — Microsoft occupies the first two).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption479.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>ONEXTweaks widget position</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption480.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Legacy (ViGEm)</value>
  </data>
  <data name="OnexCaption481.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>ViGEmBus is the old controller-emulation driver. The default backend is now VIIPER (usbip-win2), so ViGEm is optional — only install it if you switch the backend to Legacy under System → Debug. It does not affect onboarding completion while VIIPER is active.</value>
  </data>
